+# Codex review dispatch
+
+Use a new `spawn_agent` for each round, without inheriting the parent's
+conversation. If the tool exposes `fork_turns`, set it to `"none"`; if it exposes
+`fork_context`, set it to `false`. Give it only the filled reviewer prompt,
+target repository, base ref, and applicable instruction paths. Carry prior
+findings and declines only in the template's explicit fields.
+
+Use the configured session model; do not select a costlier model without the
+user's instruction. Follow the available tool schema rather than passing
+Claude `general-purpose` or `Explore` types. Wait for the complete result.
+The reviewer must read the instruction files and must not modify the repository.
+If fresh context cannot be guaranteed, report the limitation and stop the loop.
